  "reading_note": "Operation shares are STRONGLY batch dependent, so no single ranking describes the ELF training step. Muon  dominates at B=1 (61.1%) because its per-parameter work is batch-invariant while everything else is not: its absolute cost is nearly flat (73.8 / 88.6 / 86.1 ms) while the step grows 120.8 -> 298.1 -> 1162.8 ms, so its share collapses to 7.4% at B=32. Stage 0 asked whether the two auxiliary self-conditioning forwards convert their call count into wall share: combined they are 11.6% at B=1, 15.6% at B=8 and 22.8% at B=32 \u2014 real and rising, but never dominant, and always smaller than backward. This is a Stage-1 profile only; no target is selected and Stage 2 owns that decision."
